Except for the typo on a=... (need to add a ;  )

gcc -mieee file.c should do it.

$ cat test.c
int main() {
double a,b;
a=1.e-314;
b=1.;
a=a*b;
}

$ gcc -mieee -o t test.c
$ ./t
$ uname -a
Linux faure 2.0.35 #1 Wed Feb 17 15:20:33 CST 1999 alpha unknown

HTH,

B.

